@AE 155. "And ministry and faith" (Revelation 2:19) = good and truth there.

@--. The reason "ministry" = good, is that "ministry," in the Word, is said of good. Hence it is that the function of Aaron, of his sons, and of the Levites, has been called "ministry;" and, in general, [so has] the function of priests; and that by to "minister to Jehovah" or the Lord, is meant to worship Him from the good of love. Hence it is evident that, "ministry" has relation to works...

@--[2]. That "ministry," and to "minister," in the Word, are said of the good of love. Illustrated.

@--. "He shall make His ministers a flaming fire" (Psalms 104:4) = that they are recipients of the Divine good. Hence it is evident that by "ministers" are meant those who are in the good of love.

@--[3]. "Ministers of His, doing His will" (Psalms 103:21)... "Ministers" = those who are in goods.

@--[4]. "Ye shall be called the priests of Jehovah, the ministers of our God" (Isaiah 61:6). The priests are called "ministers," because they represented the Lord as to the good of love. Hence it is that those who are in the good of love, are called, in the Word, "priests." From this also it is that they are called "ministers of God." Hence it is that the function of Aaron and his sons is called "ministry"... and that to enter into the Tent of the Assembly and perform the ministry there, and also to approach the altar and perform the ministry there, is called "ministry." Illustrated.

@--[5]. Of those who are in the Celestial Kingdom, to "minister," is said... Hence it is evident what is signified by to "minister," and "a minister," in the following places. Illustrated.

@--. As to "minister" is predicated of the good of love, it is said to "minister to Jehovah"... and therefore it is said of the Lord that He "will minister."

@--[end]. (Thus) by "ministry" is signified all that is done from the good of love; thus the good of love.

@282[5]. "The rams of Nebaioth shall minister to thee" (Isaiah 60:7) = the truths which lead the life from spiritual affection.

@336[9]. To "minister" is predicated of good.

@340[6]. To "minister" = worship from spiritual good.

@409[2]. The Lord as to His Divine Human is called "Servant" and "Minister." Illustrated. @--[4].

@419[11]. By "ministers" (Psalms 104) are meant those who are in the Lord's Celestial Kingdom; and, as they are recipient of the Divine good, it is said that "He makes them a flaming fire." @504[14].

@--. That ministers are called "ministers" from the reception of Divine good. Reference.

@478[end]. Those who are in good are called in the Word "the Lord's ministers;" and [are said] to "minister to Him."

@527[5]. "With the Levites the priests My ministers" (Jeremiah 33:21) = conjunction with the Lord through Divine good.

@734[14]. The ministry of the Levites was called "warfare." Explained.

