@--[3]. "Directors." Illustrated.

@--[end]. That directors were governors of the people distinct from their princes, elders, and judges. Illustrated.

@7136. "The directors of the sons of Israel were smitten" (Exodus 5:14) = that those who proximately received and communicated the infestations were injured by the injected falsities. @7137. @7141. @7155.

@7250[end]. The Lord moderates...

@8566. That they should be more moderate in their complaints. Signified.

@LJCont 40[end]. Directors are set over the English there.

@42. Here the directors dwell. @LJPost 292.

@54[end]. I heard from a director of that society. @SE 6041[end].

@DP 77. His freedom and rationality... regulate... @--[2].

@328[7]. The presidents, the directors, the leaders in the Church...

@AR 54. The Lord moderates and tempers His Divine...

