@LJ 56[7]. (The Papists) there send forth monks, to allure the gentiles to their religiosity...

@61[6]. See <Last Judgment>.

@LJCont 78. When monks penetrate (to the Africans)... They sell them. @SE 6095[2].

@AR 294[2]. Near them were Papists with monks...

@--[11]. One of the monks arose, and said... Another monk said...

@767. By "the merchants of the earth" are meant the lower ones in the order, who are called monks.

@TCR 582. The flagellation of one monk for the whole company...

@817. The monks by clandestine arts procure a communication for themselves (with the Protestants)...

@820[2]. Converted monks there teach them...

@824. The monks especially seek there for the saints...

@SE 3597. See <Jesuit>. @DeConj 98.

@3598[end]. In Italy, where the monks insinuate themselves with wives...

@4958. They were exciting the white monks...

@5103. Under <Luther>, see this reference.

@5249. See <Last Judgment>. @5271. @5285, _et seq_., @5419. @5732. @5738.

@5450[end]. Those who were such were monks, because they keep all in... thick darkness: hence the papistical thick darkness.

@5513. a. 17. Among others who come thither are monks... They travel about in the same way in the other life...

@5833. He wondered that so many of the lower monks make themselves Christ...

@5957. Concerning a certain monk who lived in the Dark Ages...

@AE 1044. The interiors with the monks... appeared so empty that they did not know a single truth which leads to Heaven. They have been explored, and were seen to be such.

@1055. The Word is read... but little with the monks, who teach. @1062.

@LJPost 110. That they might be instructed by their own, who had been upright monks...

Monkey. See <Ape>.

Monogamist.; Monogamus.
Monogamous.; Monogamicus.
See <Wife>.

@CL 70. For monogamous marriages - which are those of one man with one wife - correspond to the marriage of the Lord and the Church...

@77[4]. We counsel you to live monogamists...

@--[5]. Therefore all of us in this Heaven are monogamists...

@141. That chastity is predicated solely of monogamous marriages, or those of one man with one wife. Explained.

@369. That spiritual jealousy exists with monogamists, and natural with polygamists. Explained.

